Translation patch: `Value::as_sql` (formatting)

Change: Each `format!(..)` becomes the call of the `sql_trusted` function for that format string (patch 80) with the same arguments (`format_i64`, `format_u64`, `format_f32`, `format_f64`, `format_date`, `format_datetime`, `format_datetime_micros`, `format_time(_neg)`, `format_time_micros(_neg)`; the hour arithmetic `days * 24 + u32::from(hours)` stays in `as_sql`); `"NULL".into()` and `String::from("0x")` become `sql_trusted::string_from_str(..)`; `from_utf8(bytes)` (`Ok`/`Err`) becomes `trusted::str_from_utf8(bytes)` (`Some`/`None`, patch 40) and the `use std::str::from_utf8` import is dropped; the hex loop `for c in bytes.iter() { s.extend(format!("{:02X}", *c).chars()) }` becomes an index loop calling `sql_trusted::string_extend_chars(&mut s, sql_trusted::format_hex_upper_02(bytes[k]))`.
Why: Aeneas does not model `fmt`/`format!`, `String`'s methods or the slice iterator (see patch 80).
Behaviour: Identical: each helper's body is the replaced expression; `trusted::str_from_utf8` is `from_utf8(..).ok()`, and the `Err` payload was unused; the bytes are visited in the same order.

